`symlink(2)` is reached here as an `extern fn`, i.e. a libSystem import
(SPEC 11.7); Bit's ELF output is fully static with no dynamic symbol table,
so this program cannot link on Linux. The stress harness skips any directory
containing this marker on a non-Darwin host. The Linux provider of
`bit_rt_fs_open_nofollow_w` is proved by its own g2archive build instead.
See _tests_/stress/fsnofollow/fsnofollow.bit.
